meta {
  name: 05-CheckProfileForBadge
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{host}}/api/users/{{amakaUserId}}/profile
  body: none
  auth: none
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.role: eq OWNER
}

docs {
  # Let me view my own public profile to see how applicants will see me
  # right now.

  ⚠️ `identityVerifiedAt` is null because Dayo hasn't approved me yet, but
  there's no field saying "submission pending". From the public's POV, my
  profile looks identical whether I never submitted or whether I'm waiting
  on review. That undermines trust both directions.

  ✅ Good news — my email and phone are correctly hidden. Only public bits.

  BLOCKED: To get my badge stamped, an admin (Dayo) has to approve my
  verification. Cross-persona dependency — I'll continue WITHOUT a badge
  and see how far I can get. Per RULES, I'll note this and move on.
}
